#Протокол_Intent_Tree_WorkGraph_Layout<[
Базис:
  Текущий work/backlog.bvc удобен как seed и MVP-очередь, но один растущий файл создаёт конфликты параллельных агентов и плохо отражает домены проекта.
  WorkGraph OS Integration Model уже зафиксировал: Work Graph/.bvc остаётся source of truth, JSON/dashboard/graph are derived projections, SQLite является optional runtime queue/index, а NoSQL не входит в MVP.
  Intent tree должен взять сильную сторону intent graph: хранить смысл по доменам, потокам и evidence/memory рядом с источником намерения, не превращая UI board или queue в canonical state.
Вектор:
  Canonical state переносится из monolithic backlog в дерево .bvc atoms под intent/, где каждый WorkItem, protocol, evidence summary and memory record lives in a small stable file.
  work/backlog.bvc становится generated/reviewable index projection: ordering, current operational queue, compact summaries and migration compatibility for existing runtime readers.
  JSON snapshots, operator dashboard snapshot and derived graph/RAG slices build from the intent tree plus optional projection indexes, not from browser state or provider sessions.
  SQLite may materialize runnable queue, run log and lookup indexes for scheduling/crash recovery, but it must be reconciled back to canonical .bvc atoms and remain rebuildable.
  Intent graph canon: protocols/intent-graph-storage-v1.bvc; roadmap view — projection выбранной ветки, не primary storage.
Цель:
  Work Graph получает storage layout, где intent tree является source of truth, а backlog, UI board, JSON snapshots, SQLite queue and graph/RAG remain replaceable projections with low merge conflict risk.

Проверки:
  описана структура папок intent tree
  backlog определён как projection/index, not canonical monolith
  JSON snapshots, SQLite and NoSQL roles separated
  migration plan preserves work.id, status, depends_on, evidence and trace refs
  concurrency benefits and conflict avoidance are explicit

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  work.source: design-intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Структура_Intent_Tree<[
Базис:
  Папки должны отражать устойчивые intent domains, а не текущую форму UI или исполнителя.
Вектор:
  intent/system/runtime/ хранит runtime, serialization, queue, worker adapter and verification loop WorkItems/protocols.
  intent/system/storage/ хранит storage decisions, migration plans, source-of-truth rules, SQLite/GBC/NoSQL deferrals and compatibility records.
  intent/ui/dashboard/ хранит operator dashboard, backlog board, graph viewer, atom inspector and UI projection WorkItems/protocols.
  intent/domains/onebase/ хранит OneBase artifact mapping, golden path, posting scenarios, verification command and domain implementation tasks.
  intent/research/pvrg/ хранит Graph/RAG, retrieval, PVRG slice and future vector/index research as derived-context design.
  intent/evidence/ хранит structured Evidence Record atoms or evidence-summary atoms when evidence graduates from legacy inline strings.
  intent/memory/ хранит Project Memory v1 records: decisions, invariants, architecture facts, domain facts, risks and open questions.
  protocols/, ui/, domains/, schemas/ and src/ remain artifact locations for human design/code; intent/ stores the canonical work/memory/evidence atoms that point to those artifacts.
Цель:
  Intent tree makes ownership visible by folder while preserving the WorkItem graph through stable ids and labels rather than file placement alone.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: intent-tree-folder-structure
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Имена_И_Связи_WorkItem_Atoms<[
Базис:
  WorkItem ids already act as durable references in depends_on, dashboard snapshots, evidence summaries and worker input.
Вектор:
  WorkItem file name SHOULD be <work.id>.work.bvc, for example intent/system/storage/design-intent-tree-workgraph-layout.work.bvc.
  One file SHOULD contain one canonical WorkItem atom during migration; companion evidence-summary or memory atoms may live beside it only with their own stable ids.
  Atom header MAY keep the existing Russian task name, but work.id is the primary machine identity and must never be regenerated during file moves.
  Required links stay in labels: work.id, work.status, work.depends_on, work.target_files, trace.status, work.next_action, work.blocker and owner/department/priority/risk where present.
  Cross-domain dependencies use work.id references, not relative file paths; optional labels such as work.path or intent.domain may accelerate projection but are rebuildable.
  Evidence links should move from free text toward evidenceIds or evidence atoms under intent/evidence/, while legacy Свидетельства lines stay preserved until Evidence v1 migration exists.
Цель:
  Moving a task between folders changes intent ownership, not identity, dependency graph or evidence trail.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: workitem-atom-naming-and-links
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Роль_Work_Backlog_Step<[
Базис:
  Current runtime and UI parse work/backlog.bvc directly, so backlog cannot disappear before reader migration.
Вектор:
  MVP after migration: work/backlog.bvc becomes an index/projection over intent/**/*.work.bvc, generated or manually refreshed in a stable order.
  It may contain compact WorkItem summaries, queue ordering, current ready/in_progress/blocked/done slices, and compatibility fields needed by parseWorkItems/buildSnapshot.
  It must not be the only place where canonical WorkItem body, status, evidence or dependency truth exists once migration completes.
  During transition, backlog may be dual-written only under explicit migration tasks; after cutover, updates should modify task files first and rebuild backlog projection.
  Runtime readers should eventually accept multiple roots or an index manifest, then treat work/backlog.bvc as a convenient snapshot source rather than the canonical monolith.
Цель:
  Existing board and tests keep working while storage moves to smaller canonical files with less merge pressure.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: backlog-as-index-projection
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#JSON_UI_And_Graph_Projections<[
Базис:
  workgraph.snapshot.v1, operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1 and derived graph viewer already define UI-facing read models.
Вектор:
  workgraph.snapshot.v1 should be built from parsed canonical WorkItems, regardless of whether the input source is work/backlog.bvc or intent/**/*.work.bvc.
  operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1 remains a derived dashboard read model with currentTasks, readyQueue, blocked, statusCounts, recentEvidence, workerRunSummaries, memoryUpdates and actionFeed.
  UI board and readonly graph viewer must read snapshots or API projections, not raw intent files in the browser.
  JSON snapshots may be written to build/cache locations or served from runtime APIs; they are deterministic exports and safe to delete/rebuild.
  Graph/RAG slices may add WorkItem, FileArtifact, Evidence, MemoryRecord, DomainObject and ProviderRun nodes, but each node needs source refs back to canonical atoms or artifacts.
Цель:
  UI and retrieval can evolve quickly while the canonical source remains inspectable .bvc atoms.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: intent-tree-json-ui-projections
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#SQLite_Runtime_Index_And_Queue<[
Базис:
  PromptPilot-style queue mechanics are useful for worker scheduling, but a queue must not become Work Graph truth.
Вектор:
  Use SQLite only when runtime needs multi-process claim coordination, durable scheduled runs, retry/rate-limit state, crash recovery, efficient polling or fast lookup by work.id/status/provider/runId.
  Suggested tables are projection-oriented: task_index(work_id, status, priority, risk, path, updated_at), run_queue(run_id, work_id, provider_id, queue_status, next_run_at, retry_count, timeout_ms), run_log(run_id, work_id, result, evidence_id, started_at, finished_at).
  SQLite rows are rebuilt or reconciled from intent tree snapshots and worker/evidence outputs; status transitions still require writing canonical WorkItem/evidence atoms.
  SQLite should not store BVC body as the only copy, hidden provider state, memory records without .bvc equivalents, or UI layout state as project truth.
Цель:
  SQLite improves local execution reliability only after scheduling needs justify it, without changing the source-of-truth model.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: sqlite-runtime-index-queue
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#NoSQL_Non_Goal_And_Revisit_Triggers<[
Базис:
  Current needs are human-readable canonical atoms, deterministic JSON projections and optional local runtime queue/index.
Вектор:
  NoSQL is a non-goal for MVP because it adds operational complexity before there is a proven need for remote collaborative writes, document-scale queries or independent service ownership.
  Do not introduce MongoDB, CouchDB, DynamoDB or similar stores for canonical WorkItems, memory, evidence, dashboard state or graph/RAG in the first storage migration.
  Revisit NoSQL only when one of these is true: multiple remote users need concurrent offline/online writes; query shape cannot be served by intent tree plus JSON/SQLite indexes; event volume exceeds local SQLite and file snapshots; deployment requires a managed remote document API; or conflict-free sync semantics become a product requirement.
  Even after revisiting, NoSQL should begin as derived or replicated storage unless a separate architecture decision replaces .bvc canonical atoms with equivalent reviewable guarantees.
Цель:
  Storage stays boring and reviewable until project scale proves that a document database solves a real bottleneck.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: nosql-non-goal-mvp
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Migration_Plan_From_Backlog_To_Task_Files<[
Базис:
  Migration must preserve existing WorkItem ids, statuses, evidence, dependencies, trace status and current UI/runtime behavior.
Вектор:
  Step 1: parse work/backlog.bvc with existing parser and create an inventory table of work.id, atomName, status, depends_on, target_files, evidence count, trace.status and proposed intent path.
  Step 2: choose deterministic placement rules by department/domain/target_files: frontend-ui -> intent/ui/dashboard, product-architecture with OneBase targets -> intent/domains/onebase, knowledge-publishing/RAG -> intent/research/pvrg or intent/memory, devops-runtime/agent-platform -> intent/system/runtime or intent/system/storage.
  Step 3: write one <work.id>.work.bvc file per task, preserving BVC, criteria, labels, Свидетельства, blocker and journal-like sections exactly enough for parse/roundtrip compatibility.
  Step 4: add or generate an index/projection at work/backlog.bvc that still contains every work.id and status until runtime readers can scan intent/**.
  Step 5: add tests for parsing both monolith and tree inputs, duplicate work.id detection, missing dependency detection and snapshot parity with the pre-migration backlog.
  Step 6: only after parity passes, update runtime/UI commands to read intent roots or a manifest first and backlog projection second.
  Step 7: record migration evidence and keep a rollback path: regenerate old monolithic backlog from task files if reader cutover fails.
Цель:
  Migration changes storage granularity without losing graph identity, operational status or evidence history.

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  plan.id: migrate-backlog-to-intent-tree
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Concurrency_And_Conflict_Avoidance<[
Базис:
  Parallel agents should not fight over one monolithic file for unrelated domains.
Вектор:
  Domain folders create natural edit ownership: UI agents touch intent/ui/dashboard, runtime agents touch intent/system/runtime, domain agents touch intent/domains/onebase, memory/retrieval agents touch intent/memory or intent/research/pvrg.
  One WorkItem per file means status/evidence edits usually conflict only when two agents operate on the same task.
  work/backlog.bvc projection can be regenerated in stable sorted order, so projection conflicts are mechanical and lower risk than semantic conflicts in canonical atoms.
  Stable work.id dependencies avoid path churn; moving a file should not require every dependent task to edit depends_on.
  Snapshot builders should detect duplicate ids, missing dependencies and stale projection entries before status transitions are accepted.
Цель:
  The storage model supports concurrent work by isolating semantic edits and making generated/index conflicts reproducible.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: intent-tree-concurrency-policy
  protocol.id: intent-tree-workgraph-layout
  trace.status: verified
]>
